      "kind": "text",
      "name": "Ordinary Memory access never grants secret access.…",
      "text": "Ordinary Memory access never grants secret access. Granting access and approving reviews are browser actions. Built-in Null has no Secrets tools. Encryption at rest protects stored data; it is not end-to-end encryption and cannot recall a value someone has already exported.",
